# Test Ratio Enforcement — MANDATORY

## The Rule

Every time you create or update tests, **ALL FOUR** of the following MUST hold individually:

```
Negative       >= 3 × Positive
Edge/Boundary  >= 3 × Positive
Functional     >= 3 × Positive
Integration    >= 3 × Positive
```

This is non-negotiable. If **any** ratio is not met, you are NOT done.

## Classification Guide

| Category | What qualifies | Examples |
|----------|---------------|----------|
| **Positive** | Happy path — feature works as designed | Valid submit succeeds, correct data returned, status changes correctly |
| **Negative** | Invalid/missing input, unauthorized, expected failures | Empty required field returns 400, deleted record not found, wrong role denied |
| **Edge/Boundary** | Boundary values, soft-delete interactions, type mismatches, fallback paths | Soft-deleted parent with active child, wrong EntityType, nullable FK edge, concurrent modification, max/min values |
| **Functional** | Business rules, validation logic, state transitions, computed values | Audit fields populated, permissions enforced, workflow transitions, data transformations |
| **Integration** | End-to-end flows, cross-service interactions, API contracts | Full CRUD through API, service-to-DB round-trip, multi-component workflows |

## Mandatory Checklist (MUST print before completing any test task)

Every time you finish creating or modifying tests, you MUST output this table:

```
### 3:1 Ratio Compliance Check
| Category          | Count | Tests                          |
|-------------------|-------|--------------------------------|
| Positive (P)      | X     | [list test names]              |
| Negative (N)      | X     | [list test names]              |
| Edge/Boundary (E) | X     | [list test names]              |
| Functional (F)    | X     | [list test names]              |
| Integration (I)   | X     | [list test names]              |
| **N ≥ 3P?**       | ✅/❌ | N >= 3 × P                     |
| **E ≥ 3P?**       | ✅/❌ | E >= 3 × P                     |
| **F ≥ 3P?**       | ✅/❌ | F >= 3 × P                     |
| **I ≥ 3P?**       | ✅/❌ | I >= 3 × P                     |
```

If **any** check is ❌, you MUST add more tests in that category before proceeding.

## Common Mistakes to Avoid

- ❌ Counting a "verify X does NOT happen" test as positive — it's negative
- ❌ Counting a "verify exact call count" test as positive — it's functional/negative
- ❌ Treating fallback/alternate-path success as positive — it's edge
- ❌ Creating tests without checking the ratio at all
- ❌ Deferring negative/edge/functional/integration tests to "later" — they must be created NOW
- ❌ Proceeding after printing a failing ratio check
- ❌ Only checking the combined (N+E) ratio — each category must pass individually
- ❌ Having fewer functional or integration tests than 3× positive
